# .claudeignore
#
# Scopes Claude's search and directory exploration away from generated /
# vendored noise. This is a discovery filter, not a security boundary --
# ignored content can still surface through direct reference, indexing, or
# system-reminder injection. For actual secrets (.env, etc.), use the
# permissions.deny block in settings.json instead -- see note at the bottom.

# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Build output
dist/
build/
.next/
out/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Test / coverage artifacts
coverage/

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Prisma -- generated migration SQL, rarely worth a broad search.
# schema.prisma itself is NOT excluded (it's outside prisma/migrations/).
prisma/migrations/

# Editor / OS noise
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

# Version control internals
.git/
